            <ArticleTitle>Effects of five years of cardiac rehabilitation after coronary artery bypass grafting on coronary risk factors.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1428-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary risk factors were studied in 119 patients randomly assigned to cardiac rehabilitation and compared with 109 patients receiving standard care alone after coronary artery bypass grafting. The long-term impact of rehabilitation on risk factors was modest in patients undergoing elective coronary surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
